## Debrief template (EDIT THIS — REQUIRED for /debrief)

> `/debrief` hard-stops until this section has a template. These are the
> questions the debrief walks after a visit, and the sentiment scale.

**Sentiment scale** — how you record "how it went":

- `great | good | mixed | rough | bad`  (default; use any scale you like)

**Debrief prompts** — asked in order after each visit:

1. **What did we actually do?** — the real work performed on-site.
2. **What did we cover?** — topics / systems / agenda items addressed.
3. **How did it go?** — the honest sentiment (from the scale above).
4. **Pros** — what went well. Be specific.
5. **Cons** — what went badly, friction, concerns. Don't soften these —
   the point of the log is that a future visit reads the honest read.
6. **Follow-ups** — each as **next-action + owner + date**. The open loop
   the practice acts on.

<!-- Tune the prompts to your practice. A strategy consult and a plumbing
     call-out share the record but not the questions. Add practice-specific
     prompts (e.g. "site-safety notes", "upsell signal", "renewal risk"). -->

