## Note on co-mounted modules

- If `rasa.module.schedule` is mounted, a scheduled booking becomes a
  `planned` visit — carry the booking id on the visit rather than
  re-entering the appointment.
- If `rasa.module.invoices` is mounted, point your billable policy at how a
  completed visit's hours become an invoice line — one source of truth for
  "how a visit bills."
- The `account: @acct-<slug>` handle is shared with every business-ops
  module; resolve display names from your account ledger if you have one.
  Do **not** seed a competing accounts registry here.
